# Rollback capture of a previous FRONTEND deploy (2026-09-05, web-frontend-lead).
# The .tar.gz is ~32 MB and is 94% the terrain file, which is already tracked in
# public/data — committing it would duplicate 30 MB of blob per release.
# THE ARCHIVE IS NOT THE AUTHORITATIVE ROLLBACK TARGET AND DOES NOT NEED TO BE:
# the previous deploy is a git commit in the site repo (aiciv-inc-site a45fdc9),
# which is what Netlify publishes from. The archive is a local belt-and-braces
# copy for the case where the site repo itself is unavailable.
# Its .sha256 IS tracked, so the archive can be authenticated if it is ever used.
deploy/previous-frontend-deploy/*.tar.gz
